# hotkeys.js/hotkeys.json are gitignored, same as lib/app-hotkeys.ahk on the Windows side — but
# unlike lib/app-hotkeys.ahk, their templates (hotkeys.template.js/hotkeys.template.json) are an
# *unsanitized* mirror of these, refreshed by dev-scripts/make-template.sh on every commit (see
# hooks/pre-commit). A git pull always brings the real, working config-as-of-the-last-commit
# along via the template, without git ever touching your own local hotkeys.js/hotkeys.json
# directly — no merge conflicts, no risk of a pull clobbering local edits you haven't committed
# anywhere, since these two are never staged/tracked at all.
linux/kwin/alttabsucks/contents/code/hotkeys.js
linux/kwin/alttabsucks/contents/code/hotkeys.json